{"results":[{"body":"R.J. Torbert is an American author and designer. He was credited with naming the Ghostface mask in the Scream franchise. Torbert joined Fun World in 1996 and was given the task of naming the mask prior to the film debut of Scream, deciding on \"Ghostface\" with the blessing of Fun World owners Stanley and Allan Geller. Torbert felt it looked like a \"ghost in pain\", believing it to be a unique ...","href":"https://scream.fandom.com/wiki/R.J._Torbert","title":"R.J. Torbert | Scream Wiki | Fandom"},{"body":"Scream (1996) - The Ghostface mask was first developed for novelty stores during the Halloween season between 1991 and 1992 by Fun World employee Brigitte Sleiertin as part of a series titled \"Fantastic Faces\", the mask itself known as \"The Peanut-Eyed Ghost\". The final design was approved by Fun World Vice President Allan Geller. Wes Craven claimed to have originally found the mask, but later ...","href":"https://m.imdb.com/title/tt0117571/trivia/?item=tr3638444","title":"Scream (1996) - Trivia - IMDb"},{"body":"First released in 1991, the mask was part of Alterian's \"Ghost Maker\" product line. Alterian alleges that the company Fun World copied this design in 1992 to create its \"Fantastic Faces\" line, which was later licensed and became the iconic mask used in the Scream film franchise.","href":"https://www.scream-thrillogy.com/2026/02/the-ghostface-files-true-origin-of.html","title":"The Ghostface Files: The True Origin of the Scream Mask"},{"body":"Torbert sat down for an in-depth interview with Examiner.com and dished the following. On how audiences have reacted to the look of GhostFace, Torbert offered: \"My opinion is that audiences had never seen a face of a ghost like this before. When the mask was developed in 1991-1992, it was part of a style assortment called Fantastic Faces.","href":"https://www.imdb.com/news/ni3723309/","title":"R.J. Torbert Talks the GhostFace Mask and Scream 4 - IMDb"},{"body":"The Ghost Face mask, an iconic symbol of horror, has a rich history that spans from its creation at Fun World to its prominent role in the Scream franchise and its presence in Halloween merchandise like the Spirit Halloween animatronic.","href":"https://holidaypaths.com/halloween/ghost-face-mask-spirit-halloween","title":"The Untold Story of the Ghost Face Mask: From Fun World Origins to ..."}]}